{"version":1,"reference":{"kind":"artifact_content","namespace":"#3451","artifact_type":"_dh-work-item-head-v1","name":"head"},"owner_reference":"#3451","content":"{\"version\":1,\"issue_reference\":\"#3451\",\"parent_revision\":\"b287e5be889f0f391daeda3124b4a62352a194b9\",\"root_revision\":\"0160b4d43ee6defd8e98c05d597a5cfbf133757f1b701780d9c55c7578a9ea6f\",\"body\":\"<!-- backlog-metadata:\\npriority: P1\\ntype: Feature\\nstatus: open\\nadded: 2026-09-06\\n-->\\n\\n## Description\\n\\nA plugin is code, and instructions as prose that sometimes call the tools that code exposes, and both feed a harness whose hooks, models and tool-calling semantics are also known. A defect can originate at any of those layers. Nothing in the backlog item schema records which layer is which, so the layer where a symptom was *noticed* becomes the layer where the fix is written.\\n\\n## Fact-Check\\n\\n<div><sub>2026-09-14T20:20:14.346076Z</sub>\\n\\nVerified 2026-09-15. Every measured number below was re-run; the command and its output are given even where the result matched. No `**Hypothesis**:` line exists in this item's description, so no claim carries a `HYPOTHESIS:` prefix.\\n\\n---\\n\\n### C1a \u2014 `**Hypothesis**` appeared in 0 of the items filed in one session\\n\\nCLAIM: \\\"Measured across the 21 items filed in one session: `**Hypothesis**` appeared in **0 of 21**\\\" (\u00a7 Why A Validated Field And Not A Documented Convention)\\nVERDICT: VERIFIED (substance), with the denominator unconfirmed\\n\\nEVIDENCE:\\n- Source: GitHub GraphQL `userContentEdits(last:1).diff`, which returns the **as-filed** body of each issue, for every issue numbered #3423\u2013#3447 (session date 2026-09-06, per \u00a7 Context \\\"session melodic-plotting-emerson, 2026-09-06\\\")\\n- Retrieved: 2026-09-15\\n- Content: |\\n    3423 ... 3446   HYPbold=0  (every row)\\n    3447            HYPbold=0\\n    # regex \\\\*\\\\*Hypothesis\\\\*\\\\* against the creation-revision body\\n    # case-insensitive /hypothesis/ anywhere in the as-filed body: also 0 for every row\\n  Result: **0 of 24** real issues in #3423\u2013#3447 carried the marker as filed (#3427 is not an issue). The first as-filed body in the whole day carrying `**Hypothesis**` is #3448, created 12:16:53Z \u2014 after the session's measurement and after the corrective edits at 12:26\u201312:37Z, and before this item (#3451) was filed at 12:57:55Z.\\n\\nCROSS_CHECK:\\n- Source: current live bodies, `gh issue list --state open --limit 2000` + `jq` regex `(?m)^\\\\*\\\\*Hypothesis\\\\*\\\\*:`\\n- Finding: #3424 and #3436 carry the marker **today** but did not as filed. Their GraphQL edit history shows body edits at 2026-09-06T12:36\u201312:37Z. A naive re-measurement against current bodies returns 1 or 2 rather than 0 \u2014 the zero is only reproducible against creation-time revisions, which is why this verdict rests on `userContentEdits`, not on `gh issue view`.\\n\\nEXPLANATION: The measurement reproduces exactly on every reconstructible window of that day's filings that closes before 12:16Z \u2014 zero, including by the loosest possible regex. The specific denominator 21 could not be pinned: the session boundary is not recorded anywhere machine-readable, and no contiguous run of 21 issues in that range is distinguishable from its neighbours. The nearest fully-reconstructible population is 23 (#3423\u2013#3446) or 24 (#3423\u2013#3447).\\n\\nCITATION: |\\n  SOURCE: GitHub GraphQL `repository.issue(number:N).userContentEdits(last:1).diff` for N in 3423..3447, Jamie-BitFlight/claude_skills (accessed 2026-09-15)\\n  VERIFIED_BY: gh api graphql + jq on 2026-09-15\\n\\n---\\n\\n### C1b \u2014 15 of 21 wrote the other label unbolded\\n\\nCLAIM: \\\"15 of 21 wrote the other label unbolded\\\" (\u00a7 Why A Validated Field And Not A Documented Convention)\\nVERDICT: REFUTED as stated; the direction it argues is understated, not overstated\\n\\nEVIDENCE:\\n- Source: same as-filed corpus, regex `(?im)^user-provided context` vs `\\\\*\\\\*User-provided context\\\\*\\\\*`\\n- Retrieved: 2026-09-15\\n- Content: |\\n    as-filed, #3423-#3446 (23 issues):  unbolded = 19,  bolded = 0,  absent = 4 (#3425,#3428,#3429,#3430)\\n    as-filed, #3423-#3447 (24 issues):  unbolded = 19,  bolded = 0,  absent = 5\\n  No window of 21 in that range yields 15. Every window yields 17 or 19.\\n\\nCROSS_CHECK:\\n- Source: `userContentEdits` edit timestamps on the affected issues\\n- Finding: 17 of the 19 unbolded items were edited at 2026-09-06T12:26\u201312:37Z to bold the label. #3437 and #3444 have `edits=0` and remain unbolded today. Verbatim proof of the flip, #3431's two revisions: creation revision `04:50:31Z` reads `User-provided context: the hook input carries \\\\`agent_id\\\\`...`; the `12:36:09Z` revision reads `**User-provided context**: the hook input carries \\\\`agent_id\\\\`...`. The two revisions are otherwise identical.\\n\\nEXPLANATION: The unbolded count reproduces as 19, not 15, on the closest reconstructible population \u2014 a higher non-compliance rate than the item claims, so the argument the number supports survives and strengthens. The \\\"15\\\" itself is not reproducible from any source available, and it is not the count of items later corrected either (that is 17).\\n\\nCITATION: |\\n  SOURCE: GitHub GraphQL userContentEdits diffs, #3423\u2013#3447 (accessed 2026-09-15); #3431 revisions 2026-09-06T04:50:31Z and 2026-09-06T12:36:09Z\\n  VERIFIED_BY: gh api graphql + jq on 2026-09-15\\n\\n---\\n\\n### C1c \u2014 Reconciling the session measurement with the Research section's whole-backlog count\\n\\nCLAIM: Implicit in the item carrying both figures \u2014 \u00a7 Why A Validated Field says 0 of 21; \u00a7 Research says \\\"10 of 663 open items carry a line-initial `**Hypothesis**:`\\\", and labels the pair `[CONFLICT] ... [RESOLVED] Different populations`.\\nVERDICT: VERIFIED \u2014 the Research figure re-runs exactly, and the two measure different things. Neither replaces the other.\\n\\nEVIDENCE:\\n- Source: `gh issue list -R Jamie-BitFlight/claude_skills --state open --limit 2000 --json number,body,labels` then `jq` with `(?m)^\\\\*\\\\*Hypothesis\\\\*\\\\*:`\\n- Retrieved: 2026-09-15\\n- Content: |\\n    open_total: 663\\n    line-initial **Hypothesis**:: 10\\n      numbers: 3298, 3305, 3322, 3325, 3326, 3328, 3424, 3436, 3448, 3454\\n    naive **Hypothesis**: 12\\n  Every figure in the Research section's table \u2014 663, 10, the exact ten issue numbers, and the naive-vs-anchored 12/10 caveat \u2014 reproduces byte-for-byte.\\n\\nCROSS_CHECK:\\n- Source: the as-filed corpus from C1a/C1b\\n- Finding: two of the ten (#3424, #3436) acquired the marker by later edit, not at filing. So the two measurements differ on **three** axes, not one: population (one session's filings vs all currently-open items), revision (creation-time body vs current body), and regex (any `**Hypothesis**` vs line-initial `**Hypothesis**:`).\\n\\nEXPLANATION: The Research count measures marker presence in the live backlog today; the \u00a7 Why A Validated Field count measures compliance at the moment of writing. The item's own `[RESOLVED]` note is correct that they are different populations, and understates it \u2014 they are also different revisions of the same items, which is why the same items can read 0 on one and non-zero on the other.\\n\\nCITATION: |\\n  SOURCE: gh issue list, Jamie-BitFlight/claude_skills, 663 open items (accessed 2026-09-15)\\n  VERIFIED_BY: gh + jq on 2026-09-15\\n\\n---\\n\\n### C2a \u2014 Evidence table row (2026-09-15): 19 rule pointers, `.codex/hooks.json`, and the #3446/#3437 timeline\\n\\nCLAIM: \\\"Non-Claude harnesses lost 19 rule pointers when `AGENTS.md` was culled | prose in `AGENTS.md`, telling those harnesses to go read the rule index | the hook wiring \u2014 `.codex/hooks.json` already runs four Codex events, and #3446 already recorded that both harnesses support plugin-bundled hooks\\\" + \\\"the correction was