enforcement topology. Three candidate enforcement points exist, with disjoint caller sets. The Research section settled what each does on failure; this analysis adds who traverses each.\\n\\n| Candidate enforcement point | Layer | Behaviour on failure (per Research \u00a7RT-ICA #7) | Callers that traverse it |\\n|---|---|---|---|\\n| `operations.add_item`'s argument validators (`operations.py:1356-1401`) | Python | Refuse \u2014 `ValidationError` before storage | Every writer on every backend: `backlog_add` MCP tool, `backlog add` CLI, every agent and skill that files an item, `backlog-sync.yml`. Complete coverage. |\\n| `finalize.md`'s Output Validation Gate (`finalize.md:125-134`) | Agent-executed prose | Retry \u00d73 same model, then `status=blocked` | Only the `work-backlog-item` groom route. Not `--quick` (`quick/start.md`, which `AGENTS.md` prescribes for one-file fixes), not `groom-backlog-item`'s own copy, not GitHub round-trip, not direct `backlog_groom` calls. |\\n| `_normalize_section_key` / section registry (`operations.py:978-1014`) | Python, split | `\\\"Description\\\"` refuses; any other unregistered name warns-and-stores; `github_sync.py:300-301` stores silently with no warning | Local-write callers get the warning (and only when `output=` is threaded \u2014 `operations.py:1244` does not). GitHub-parse callers get nothing. |\\n\\nA fourth point exists that the item and artifact do not name, and it is the only one that already crosses from code into prose: `tests/test_section_name_registry_drift.py` parses every `agents/*.md` and `skills/**/*.md` for `section=\\\"X\\\"` / `sections[\\\"X\\\"]` and fails CI when a referenced name does not round-trip through `SECTION_HEADING`. Its caller set is the entire prose corpus, enforced by Python.\\n\\n### Code - Producers\\n\\n- `plugins/development-harness/backlog_core/models.py::BacklogItemMetadata` - Declares the creation-stage item schema. `layer: str = \\\"\\\"` at line 861 is already the SDLC 0/1/2 axis