eld, this is the write-path gate. Its warning reaches a structured caller only on paths that thread `output=`; `_handle_update_groomed` (line 1244) does not. | Risk: HIGH | Why: warn-and-store is the #2974 failure shape the item's own non-functional requirement forbids repeating, and the conditional `output=` threading means the signal is already lost on one of three write paths.\\n- `plugins/development-harness/backlog_core/section_registry.py::SectionKey` / `_SECTION_DISPLAY` - Lines 65-133. Any new canonical section name for the attribution must be appended here plus its display row, or it stores under `unknown__` and reads back absent. | Risk: MEDIUM | Why: mechanical addition with a documented procedure and a guarding test, but omitting it produces silent data loss rather than an error.\\n- `plugins/development-harness/backlog_core/parsing.py::build_issue_body` - Lines 592-629 deliberately emit no Story and no Acceptance Criteria because \\\"a template-filled section emitted at creation satisfies that check without anyone having written a criterion.\\\" This is the repo's own statement of the mechanical-fill failure mode the item's Open Question names. If the attribution is emitted at creation, this docstring's reasoning must be either followed or explicitly overruled. | Risk: MEDIUM | Why: a template-emitted attribution defeats a presence check by construction; the producer already documents why.\\n- `plugins/development-harness/sam_schema/core/models.py::IssueClassification` / `AnalysisMethod` - StrEnums carrying `procedural | defect | recurring-pattern | missing-guardrail | unbounded-design` and `none | 5-whys | 6-sigma | design-framing` on the SAM `Task` model. This is the same taxonomy `agents/classifier.md` writes into the `Issue Classification` prose section \u2014 already validated in code, on a different record. | Risk: MEDIUM | Why: an attribution enum added to the item model without reconciling against this one creates two classification vocabularies